message: "If you use Paralingo in your work, please cite it as below and credit the original author."
title: "Paralingo: a shared speech-analysis file for AI voice agents"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Namash"
    family-names: "Aggarwal"
    website: "https://github.com/namashworks"
repository-code: "https://github.com/namashworks/paralingo"
url: "https://github.com/namashworks/paralingo"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-10"
keywords:
  - voice agents
  - speech analysis
  - prosody
  - emotion recognition
  - conversational AI
  - MCP
abstract: >-
  A per-speaker JSON file and Python toolkit that AI voice agents read and write to
  track how a person speaks: pitch, pauses, pace, voice quality, fluency, emotion,
  communication skills, accent and non-diagnostic speech indicators, with a personal
  baseline, longitudinal trends and concrete guidance for the agent.
